Cedar Park, TX -- LinuxElectrons™ eStore has announced the availability
of an Intel Centrino based laptop pre-installed with the Fedora Core 2
Linux® operating system. Other Linux® operating systems can be installed
upon request.

Features

# Pentium M processor 1.5 GHz
# 512 MB DDR333 System Memory
# 40 GB IDE Drive
# DVD-R/CD-RW Combo
# 15.4" WXGA/WSXGA+ 256K Color Max
# Intel 855 PM Chipset
# Intel PRO/Wireless 2100 Network Connection
# ATI Mobility RADEON 9600 64MB
# PortBar III Support
# Touchpad lock support
# Carrying case is included

The M6000N implements Intel Centrino Mobile Technology, which includes Intel Pentium M processor, 855PM chipset and Intel PRO/Wireless 2100 network connection system, to deliver the most advanced mobile performance. Teamed with built-in Gigabit LAN, the notebook ensures robust and high-speed connection for wired and wireless environments.

"This laptop offers tremendous value and features for a very good price. Our research shows that a similar configured laptop from Tier 1 OEM's cost as much as $400.00 or more" said Robert Thomas, General Manager of LinuxElectrons™ eStore.

Availability

The laptop is available now and can be purchased online at:
http://store.linuxelectrons.com/product_info.php?products_id=286

About LinuxElectrons™ eStore

LinuxElectrons™ eStore features hardware and software products for the
Linux® operating system. Our staff can custom build workstations, servers
and laptops to your specifications. Additionally, the eStore staff
(computer industry veterans) is available to assist you in providing the
best Linux® hardware/software solutions for your organization.

http://store.linuxelectrons.com

