Version 0.2.7 of Real Poker has been released.  Real Poker is a
work-in-progress simulation of poker.

Real Poker is available for download at:
http://sourceforge.net/projects/realpoker

The changes from the previous release of Real Poker are:

 .added preference to allow user to decide whether or not to show the
    starting cards in the results of game simulations
 .removed the preference to show starting hands by individual cards
    (showing starting hands by individual cards is overkill and slows
    down processing)
 .added game simulations with robot players having a limited capacity
 .new format for Game Library
 .new format for .rprc file
 .newly working functions:
    Misc->Stats ... see (some) stats from learning and from simulations
    Misc->Game Library->Delete Game ... mark a game for deletion
    Misc->Game Library->Undelete Game ... remove deletion mark from game
    Misc->Game Library->Learn Game ... collect data to enable robot
                                       players to learn to play a game
    Misc->Player Library->Save Library ... save player library
    Misc->Player Library->Delete Player ... mark a player for deletion
    Misc->Player Library->Undelete Player ... remove deletion mark from player
    Misc->Player Library->Edit Player ... load highlighted player for editing
    Misc->Player Library->Create Player ... create a player
    Misc->Player Library->Dismiss ... exit from the Player Library function
    Game->Select Players ... select one or more players (to use in
                             game simulations)
 .fixed problem in counts with straights and straight flushes never losing
 .added some sounds & a preference item for playing sounds
 .numerous minor improvements
 .numerous minor bug fixes

